A||||4||gmata||Replacing Lifters||||5||
Z||000000||gmata||03-14-2001||11:57 AM||||I want to replace my lifters (V6), since one of them is making a noise when I first start up the car.  I got an estimate of $700.00 to replace all of the lifters. ( $80 parts & $620 labor).  What is the average cost of replacing the filters?||||reg||5
Z||000001||tgowens||03-14-2001||03:42 PM||||the shop time manuals call for 8 to 10.5 hours to remove and replace the heads so that rate sounds about right to me.........same with the parts cost -- that is a reasonable price in my opinion.........||||reg||1
Z||000002||GT GT 87||03-14-2001||04:14 PM||||You don't have to take of the heads to change lifters...........Steve||||reg||1
Z||000003||JC Webb||03-14-2001||06:15 PM||||Holy Cow!  $700 is outrageous!  You might as well go ahead and rebuild the entire engine if you are going to spend $700 toward lifters.  As a matter of fact you could buy a 3.4 from a junk yard for that price!  Shop around, I am positive you will find a lower estimate.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Nashco||03-14-2001||06:42 PM||||Whoa...I sure hope you wouldn't pay that much for a noisy lifter to be replaced.  If it really bothers you that much, you should save up a little more and just get a rebuild at the same time.  Since you have a worn lifter I am assuming the motor has some wear and tear.  The lifters can be removed without removing the heads, but you would have to get a buddy to do it that way, as the shop charges flat rate.  Even though the mechanic can perform a magic trick and do it without removing the heads, that's what the book calls for.  (I've seen mechanics be blessed or beaten by flat rate, so don't think you're getting ripped off)<P>So, if you <B>really</B> want that lifter fixed, ask around and find a good backyard mechanic, or a mechanic who is willing to do a side job.  They can do it without pulling the heads, and for quite a bit less.  If you can live with the noise for a while, I'd start preparing for a rebuild and get the whole ball of wax at once.<P>Just my opinion, good luck!<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||11
